# Operations Registry

- `src/services/operationsRegistry/` is the public module for production Agent, Merchant, Source Company, Source Granularity, and Granot CRM source lifecycle catalog behavior. Routes and runtime consumers use its exported commands, queries, and resolvers rather than importing registry models. `GranotCrmSource` is the only semantic registry for a Granot source label; runtime policy reads go through `src/services/granotLifecycle/sourcePolicy.ts`.
- Registry mutations require a verified signed Owner actor. Canonical signing includes admin ID, normalized email, role, timestamp, request ID, HTTP method, and path using `VANTAGE_ADMIN_PROXY_SIGNING_SECRET`. Unsigned preview compatibility must remain narrowly scoped and fail closed for production mutations.
- Every domain mutation and `operations_registry_changes` insert shares one Mongo transaction. Audit failure aborts the mutation. Cache invalidation occurs only after commit.
- Registry audit snapshots and metadata must be bounded and redact secrets, credentials, tokens, authorization values, and provider payloads.
- No registry workflow hard-deletes records. Inactive records are hidden from automatic/default selection but may be explicitly included for Owner correction workflows.
- `granot_identity.username` is authoritative after M2; `granot_crm_username` remains a temporary read fallback. Automatic Granot receiver matching is active-only.
- `lead_source_granularities` is authoritative after M3. `LeadSourceCompany.granularities[]` and default key fields remain read-only compatibility data and must not become a second writable authority.
- Source exact identifiers fail on ambiguity. Fallback aliases choose one highest-priority active candidate and fail on an equal-priority tie.
- Migration scripts under `scripts/migrations/` are dry-run by default, reject historical/unknown databases, require explicit production apply confirmation, write deterministic redacted manifests, and never import historical models.
- Required configuration shape: `VANTAGE_ADMIN_PROXY_SIGNING_SECRET`; optional replay-window override and preview compatibility settings are owned by `src/services/operationsRegistry/config.ts`. Never document secret values.
